// The prototype's other kinds: a ctx parameter that must be the
// unmodified context, nullable memory used without a test, a NULL
// passed where non-null is declared, and trusted and untrusted
// kernel pointers. A koit global function takes scalars and `ref`
// places, which are never null and never the context, so the first
// three are unwritable; the kernel-pointer parameters wait for the
// kernel-memory extension. In C:
//
//   foo((char *)ctx + 8);            /* modified ctx ptr */
//   int foo(int *p) { return *p; }   /* mem_or_null read */
